  "reason": "The current best configuration is config_031 (scVI RNA, ResNet image, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted fusion) with 0.678 accuracy and 0.646 F1, clearly improving over the same setting with PCA RNA in config_019. The remaining uncertainty in this strong lineage is whether a stronger image encoder helps when combined with scVI: under PCA, ResNet and ViT were very close (config_019 vs config_025), so the image-encoder effect is still unclear. config_037 changes only the image encoder from ResNet to imagenet_vit_l while keeping scVI, multiprofile, avgpool, and weighted fusion, isolating the image representation effect. This is the best next experiment because it exploits the best known setting, may yield a new best, and completes a clean RNA/image encoder comparison without changing multiple factors at once."
}

